==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|parede}}, from {{inh|pt|LL.|pares|parētem}}, from {{inh|pt|la|paries|parietem|g=m}}. Compare {{cog|gl|parede}}, {{cog|es|pared}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{pt-IPA|parêde}}
* {{a|Northeast Brazil}} {{IPA|pt|/pa.ˈɾe.dɪ/}}
* {{hyphenation|pt|pa|re|de}}
* {{audio|pt|pt-pt-parede.ogg|Audio (Portugal)}}

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|f}}

# [[wall]] (of a [[house]] or [[building]])

====Usage notes====
* Portuguese differentiates between external and internal walls. The barrier that surrounds and divides lands is called {{m|pt|muro}}, while the structures that make the outer part of a building and divide its rooms are called {{m|pt|parede}}.

